      en: "The Gakara Rare Earth Mines are located in Bujumbura Rural Province, western Burundi. The deposit is one of the richest rare earth deposits globally. Mining began in 2017 via a Canadian-Burundian joint venture. It produces concentrates of neodymium, praseodymium, and dysprosium. Estimated resources are about 1.5 million tons of ore. The operation creates local employment and generates foreign exchange.",
